# Equinox judges Cleansing on a board where a player's first choice already has far more answers than a speculation
# follows (KI-179): Bot2, whose turn it is and who is asked first, has 5 life and could pay for up to five of the
# seventeen lands, in more than 800,000 ways. The speculation needs only the way no one pays, which it visits first
# (`Query::speculate_resolution`, depth first, a choice of lands offering none first): Cleansing would then destroy all
# ten of Bot1's lands, more than the 6 life the players could pay for them, so every way it could go destroys one, and it
# is countered (CR 608.2, 118.12a, 119.4; the owner's rule for Cleansing). No one is asked anything, and every land stays.

